                "text": "Not examined: the check `config.secrets-file-committed` — This folder is not a git repository, so `sv` cannot say whether a secrets file was ever committed. Putting the app in git (version control, which keeps every saved version) makes this check run, and is worth doing anyway. Ask your AI coding tool to do it, and to add a .gitignore that leaves out .env and other secret files before the first commit, so that commit does not save them. If the app is already kept in version control somewhere else, that copy's history is still unchecked."
              }
